WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:06.132
Now, a miracle is about to be
created upon this planet.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.844
One hot summer day...

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.615
...I died.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.415
And then I saw...

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.222
...the future of this planet
as it faced its death.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.201
Juna!

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.396
Tokio!

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.984
Why kill?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.612
Huh? If I don't, then what'll
happen to the Earth?!

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.983
Why kill?

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.791
What are you talking about?

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.725
You told me to protect the Earth!

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.051
You fool.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.265
I didn't tell you to protect
the Earth.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:05.959
Huh?!

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:18.175
Are you sure she's the right one?

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:22.215
Her mind and spirit are
all totally in pieces.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:25.051
And she can't make out
what you...

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.019
...tell her through your telepathy.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.352
I have no choice.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.182
Juna, the Avatar of Time...

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.692
...does not even have the sense of taste.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:40.633
As she is now, she does not
recognize the taste...

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.569
...of the foods she can eat
in order to survive.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:52.139
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.180
Episode 4: Transmigration

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.670
Come on. You're so useless!

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.338
Give me a break.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.440
I was so worried about you...

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.238
...that I wasn't thinking about
how much gas I had.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.314
Oh, no.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.283
I forgot which way to go.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.807
What? Are you serious?

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.553
Are you lost?

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.989
You're always at a loss
as to which road to take.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.959
Chris? Hey, have you been
watching us all this time?

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.060
What's the matter?

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.527
Is it that guy again?

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:26.806
I was a little worried about you.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:31.072
Then, why don't you just tell me
which way I'm supposed to go?!

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.147
Tell me, tell me, huh?

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.549
Why do you think
you have that power?

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.208
Huh?

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.375
Try to figure it out on your own.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.684
What?

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.857
Cold-blooded bastard!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.428
Are you all right?

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.021
What do you want?!

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.834
You're going to be left behind.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.538
What the heck...?

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.884
Those guys are
pretty darn annoying.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.255
Why do they make you do
as they say?

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.849
What the hell happened anyway?

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.215
Back then...

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.187
...when I was dying
because of that accident...

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.657
...I saw it.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.735
The sight of this Earth...

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.966
...being degraded and poisoned
everywhere.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.832
Earth?

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:38.042
That's when that guy Chris
showed up and said that...

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:42.248
...if I was willing to
protect this planet...

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.684
...he would give me my life back.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.208
Your life?

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.183
You mean that kid back there?

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.624
You don't have to believe me.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.922
I... just didn't want to...

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.321
Didn't want to?

00:04:55.528 --> 00:05:01.023
I just couldn't bear the thought of
never seeing you and Mom again.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.735
Juna...

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.742
But, why you?

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:13.337
Why do you have to do it?
I'm sure they've got others.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:18.611
Even now,
I can sometimes hear it.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.785
The screams of the Earth.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.659
Aren't you just imagining that?

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.524
I don't hear anything.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:30.396
But...

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.265
I couldn't stand it...

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:35.723
...if you really died...

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.134
Tokio...

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.980
How unusual nowadays.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.416
Running away and eloping...

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.111
Eloping?!

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.711
What do you think you're doing?!

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:00.126
Still too young to be eloping.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.127
What the...?!

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:04.460
What're you trying to pull,
you pervert?!

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.369
Look at that. Pretty bad shape.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.912
It's like no one lives here.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.714
You think this is wise?

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.807
Following that old man like this?

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.093
Those who don't work don't eat.

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.025
Huh?

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.296
If you want to eat, then work.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.297
Work?

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:41.061
First you can collect
the vegetables.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:44.129
Collect what?
Where are the vegetables?

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:48.332
Are your eyes nothing but
empty sockets?

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.343
You watch nothing but TV...

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.578
...so you don't see things anymore.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.045
Empty sockets?

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.092
What's up?! Those guys again?

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.460
Those guys?

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.229
Some kind of ghost-like figure.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:11.856
Ghost?

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:13.998
J-Just in there...

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.836
I don't see anything.

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:21.504
B-But I'm sure I saw it right there.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:24.903
Huh?

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:29.078
It's just a cucumber.

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:35.121
No way!
This is a vegetable garden?

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:37.623
Quite lively in there, isn't it?

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.426
You've got your cucumbers,
squash, eggplant...

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:44.597
...cabbage, corn, soy beans,
and even tomatoes.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:47.191
Wow, that looks great!

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.799
Watch it. That's asparagus.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:53.366
This is asparagus?

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.400
So it is.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.213
But this is pretty bad.

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:02.147
These weeds are out of control.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.918
Why don't you do a little weeding?

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:08.521
Why should I do any weeding?

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:09.422
Huh?

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:12.516
We even have to weed
the flower garden at school.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.024
The flowers and vegetables would
lose out against the weeds, huh?

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:22.468
But do you think my vegetables
are losing out against the weeds?

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.459
Aren't they growing strong and healthy?

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:27.240
Oh, yeah...

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.442
Do you see that it's real?

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:33.674
Do you see that what you see
before you is real, young lady?

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:35.181
Real?

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.749
Boy, oh, boy...

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.985
There're bugs all over these.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:41.621
Excuse me, but the bugs
are eating your vegetables.

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:44.283
Yes, they seem to be eating well.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:45.485
Huh?

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.462
This old man's bad news.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:51.396
There's something wrong with him.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:55.492
These darn bugs!

00:08:59.105 --> 00:08:59.672
There! There! There!

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.435
Why do you kill?

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.843
But the bugs are...

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:05.640
Why do you kill?

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.546
Why do you kill?

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:11.013
Why do you kill?

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:15.521
I mean, if the bugs
eat up your vegetables...

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.290
Bugs get hungry, too.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.088
But, then, what about people...?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.397
Why do the insects
eat the vegetables?

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:29.135
Until you're able to answer that,
you don't get anything to eat.

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:30.193
What?!

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:54.527
Bathroom?
Go out to the woods in the back.

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:55.194
What?!

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:57.830
We came all the way out
to your house.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.789
What comes from the land,
ought to be returned to the land.

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:20.374
Sayuri and everyone must be
pretty worried about us by now.

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:26.352
Hey, Tokio.

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:28.027
Why do insects...

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:31.163
...know which weeds and
vegetables they can eat?

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:32.460
Right.

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.334
Here we go again with your
"Why do...?" disease.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:36.369
Think about it.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:38.971
All the grasses look
the same to me...

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.674
...but the bugs know exactly
what they're after.

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:44.768
I say it's probably instinct.

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:47.805
But I didn't know anything.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.650
When I was left in the mountains...

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.486
...I didn't know what I could eat.

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:55.579
I didn't know anything.

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:58.190
Well, that can't be helped.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.226
Human beings aren't like insects.

00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:02.161
You think?

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:05.688
You really think we're different?
Humans and insects?

00:11:10.436 --> 00:11:12.495
Well, they probably like it.

00:11:12.705 --> 00:11:16.402
They find the leaves that are tasty
and they eat them.

00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:19.334
Here we go again with
your "they like it".

00:11:20.713 --> 00:11:22.615
But I mean it.

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:25.379
I've always liked you a lot.

00:11:33.259 --> 00:11:34.692
Darn!

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.220
Why, you!

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.774
What's up?

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:01.679
No way...

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:06.892
It looks like the insects only
eat the dark parts of the leaves.

00:12:06.892 --> 00:12:09.520
Dark? What'd you mean?

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.204
Could it be that the insects
start by eating the weaker...

00:12:18.204 --> 00:12:21.002
...or bad parts of the leaves first?

00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:24.371
You're half-right.

00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:27.678
What do you mean, half-right?

00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:33.152
There was no such thing as good
or bad in the world originally.

00:12:33.152 --> 00:12:37.623
But I wonder what it is
that you felt was bad.

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:40.387
Were you just referring
to the leaves?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:45.224
Or was there an
even bigger reason?

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:49.757
You're going to have to
find the answers yourself.

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:51.869
You're so mean.

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:56.675
But I'll give you a break this time
and feed you.

00:12:56.675 --> 00:12:57.309
Really?!

00:12:57.309 --> 00:12:58.410
All right!

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.813
Tomorrow morning, though.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.314
Tomorrow?

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:05.751
I only have two meals a day.
Beyond that, it's just a waste.

00:13:05.751 --> 00:13:07.446
What...?

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:11.784
Kojiro knows how to read people.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:16.894
What's the matter?!

00:13:17.396 --> 00:13:20.559
Again...
That shadow again...

00:13:39.185 --> 00:13:42.279
No... Please don't come...

00:13:42.721 --> 00:13:44.123
Juna...

00:13:44.123 --> 00:13:49.254
Young man, you're going to be
facing tough times ahead.

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:51.664
The young lady seems to be...

00:13:51.664 --> 00:13:56.168
...able to see all kinds of things,
even though she is so young.

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:57.795
Huh? See things?

00:13:59.605 --> 00:14:01.630
You must protect her.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.375
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:14:19.658 --> 00:14:23.992
Put a little more muscle into it,
if you want to impress your girl.

00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:26.765
Perverted old man...

00:14:35.474 --> 00:14:38.136
Hey, is this grass really edible?

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:41.809
Even vegetables were once
just weeds, you know.

00:14:44.516 --> 00:14:46.814
Thanks for the breakfast!

00:14:48.554 --> 00:14:50.322
This rice is so hard!

00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:51.380
Huh?

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:54.827
It sure is.

00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:56.996
It's hulled red-kerneled rice.

00:14:56.996 --> 00:15:00.124
Chew it well and it'll
start to taste better.

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:11.710
Hey, this isn't too bad.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.979
Yeah. It's really good.

00:15:13.979 --> 00:15:16.379
All right. I'm going to dig in.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:18.846
Me, too!

00:15:24.123 --> 00:15:25.750
- Wh-Why?
- Juna?

00:15:25.824 --> 00:15:27.121
That shadow again.

00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:37.732
- What're you doing?!
- Quiet!

00:15:39.872 --> 00:15:45.139
Now, take a nice big deep breath.

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:49.748
Breathe from deep down
in your belly.

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:50.874
Right.

00:15:54.653 --> 00:15:56.985
- Breathe deeper.
- Huh?

00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:00.391
Open up your heart.

00:16:52.344 --> 00:16:54.113
Why am I...?

00:16:54.113 --> 00:16:55.410
What?

00:17:02.287 --> 00:17:03.311
Tokio...?

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:16.001
No way...

00:17:16.001 --> 00:17:18.871
Is this all me? Is this me?

00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:20.304
You?

00:17:20.672 --> 00:17:22.241
I can see it.

00:17:22.241 --> 00:17:24.903
I can see my image in the food.

00:17:25.144 --> 00:17:26.076
Huh?

00:17:26.278 --> 00:17:29.248
I can see the images of myself...

00:17:29.248 --> 00:17:33.446
...you, and even the old man
in the food.

00:17:35.421 --> 00:17:38.117
Are you sure you're all right?

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:43.862
I see. You've got good eyes.

00:17:43.862 --> 00:17:44.954
What?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:49.368
This food, the fish and vegetables...

00:17:49.368 --> 00:17:52.871
...will soon be ingested by you,
chewed...

00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:55.074
...digested, absorbed...

00:17:55.074 --> 00:17:58.874
...and will eventually become
a part of your own body.

00:17:59.344 --> 00:18:02.177
It's going to be part of
my body soon...

00:18:03.782 --> 00:18:04.917
Then...

00:18:04.917 --> 00:18:07.477
...the figure I saw yesterday
in the garden must've been...

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:14.259
Eventually it will become
a part of your body...

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.562
...and mine and the young man's.

00:18:16.562 --> 00:18:19.156
It represents the future of us.

00:18:20.132 --> 00:18:21.929
The future of my form...

00:18:24.002 --> 00:18:26.197
It is not to shoot the target.

00:18:26.538 --> 00:18:28.607
But rather to become...

00:18:28.607 --> 00:18:30.507
...one with the target.

00:18:52.331 --> 00:18:56.893
All of the food becomes me...
Becomes me...

00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:00.931
Thanks for the food!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:07.913
The squash and tomatoes
and cabbage...

00:19:07.913 --> 00:19:10.939
They all represent the
future of us!

00:19:19.658 --> 00:19:21.250
It's a rice paddy.

00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:31.302
That tickles!

00:19:47.786 --> 00:19:50.789
Wow, look at all the fields.

00:19:50.789 --> 00:19:53.025
Killing no insects or weeds...

00:19:53.025 --> 00:19:56.795
...needing no fertilizer or tilling...

00:19:56.795 --> 00:19:59.631
...fields tended by the organisms
living in them.

00:19:59.631 --> 00:20:01.599
No tilling?

00:20:12.811 --> 00:20:14.972
The wind blows...

00:20:19.251 --> 00:20:20.878
The insects dance...

00:20:25.958 --> 00:20:27.585
Time passes...

00:20:46.612 --> 00:20:49.281
The tiny lives...

00:20:49.281 --> 00:20:51.943
...till the land on their own...

00:20:52.951 --> 00:20:56.216
...and create new life.

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:07.224
Juna...

00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:18.865
I gave up my career and my
home, but not this one.

00:22:19.738 --> 00:22:21.603
Gave up your career and home?

00:22:23.175 --> 00:22:24.472
It's all in the past.

00:22:33.085 --> 00:22:35.520
Actually, I don't think I will.

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:38.683
I've got to go along with her
at least for a while.

00:22:40.759 --> 00:22:43.057
How long will it last?

00:22:44.629 --> 00:22:46.995
Just an old man talking to himself.

00:23:01.279 --> 00:23:02.177
No!

00:23:02.681 --> 00:23:03.782
What?!

00:23:03.782 --> 00:23:04.840
Run!

00:23:05.384 --> 00:23:07.753
If you don't hang onto her...

00:23:07.753 --> 00:23:10.088
...there's no telling where she'll go!

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:11.490
Right!

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.082
Juna!

00:23:23.034 --> 00:23:24.228
Oh, no!

00:23:30.709 --> 00:23:32.404
Juna!

00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:39.509
Stop it!

00:23:40.285 --> 00:23:41.887
Let go of me! Raajas...!

00:23:41.887 --> 00:23:44.589
No! That's no monster!

00:23:44.589 --> 00:23:45.521
What?

00:23:50.061 --> 00:23:50.959
No way...

00:24:14.186 --> 00:24:14.948
Juna...

00:24:18.056 --> 00:24:20.183
So they did it again, huh?

00:24:20.425 --> 00:24:21.357
Again?

00:24:22.794 --> 00:24:26.286
Why? Why do they have to kill?

00:24:26.598 --> 00:24:28.166
The insects and the weeds...

00:24:28.166 --> 00:24:31.158
...are nurturing the rice
and vegetables together.

00:24:32.204 --> 00:24:33.865
They've forgotten.

00:24:34.239 --> 00:24:37.409
Blinded by short term efficiency,
and a mistaken sense...

00:24:37.409 --> 00:24:38.671
...of good appearance.

00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:41.780
They've forgotten that the weeds,
insects and all of the land...

00:24:41.780 --> 00:24:44.544
...represent their future.

00:24:45.984 --> 00:24:47.315
Why?

00:24:48.220 --> 00:24:50.586
Why has everyone forgotten?

00:24:51.623 --> 00:24:55.024
Maybe because people are
too busy.

00:24:58.763 --> 00:25:02.367
Busy with exams,
work and study.

00:25:02.367 --> 00:25:05.637
As people get caught up with
the time on the clock...

00:25:05.637 --> 00:25:08.970
...they forget the real now.

00:25:11.843 --> 00:25:14.038
The real now...

00:25:15.847 --> 00:25:18.884
The insects, weeds and the land...

00:25:18.884 --> 00:25:21.887
...as well as human beings,
become one.

00:25:21.887 --> 00:25:24.048
That's the real now.

00:25:26.958 --> 00:25:29.950
The real now...

00:25:31.830 --> 00:25:36.801
I don't know what will happen

00:25:36.801 --> 00:25:41.439
I cry out loud

00:25:41.439 --> 00:25:44.142
Please

00:25:44.142 --> 00:25:51.105
Don't leave me alone

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:57.389
Life can be disappointing

00:25:57.389 --> 00:26:01.860
You are really gone

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.365
I want you to hold me again

00:26:07.365 --> 00:26:16.069
Only you were my angel

00:26:17.042 --> 00:26:24.346
The wind blows, and like wings...

00:26:24.649 --> 00:26:29.220
...it wraps me in sadness

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:32.457
It flies me away

00:26:32.457 --> 00:26:39.989
The air and the stars... only the frail things...

00:26:40.231 --> 00:26:44.669
...gather here... to a pure place...

00:26:44.669 --> 00:26:52.041
...to a place no one knows

00:26:56.948 --> 00:27:01.976
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:27:05.991 --> 00:27:10.325
Intermission

00:27:13.832 --> 00:27:17.700
Fields that need no tilling...

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:20.494
But why?

00:27:21.172 --> 00:27:24.009
If fields don't need to be tilled...

00:27:24.009 --> 00:27:27.342
...why do people do it anyway?

00:27:28.079 --> 00:27:29.808
Why do you think?

00:27:31.416 --> 00:27:33.008
Well...

00:27:33.251 --> 00:27:37.847
...isn't it because there's a
better yield if you till the soil?

00:27:38.089 --> 00:27:42.458
It's true that if you till the soil, you
can increase the yield slightly.

00:27:42.661 --> 00:27:44.896
By using up the
reserve of nutrients...

00:27:44.896 --> 00:27:48.059
...that were accumulated
in the soil.

00:27:48.266 --> 00:27:51.133
But that won't last forever.

00:27:51.336 --> 00:27:53.463
Huh? Why?

00:27:53.772 --> 00:27:57.142
The soil will die if you
till it too much.

00:27:57.142 --> 00:27:58.905
The soil will die?

00:27:59.577 --> 00:28:03.281
That's because the world
of the bugs, worms...

00:28:03.281 --> 00:28:07.052
...and the tiniest creatures in
the soil that you can't even see...

00:28:07.052 --> 00:28:08.753
...is destroyed.

00:28:08.753 --> 00:28:09.344
Huh?

00:28:09.921 --> 00:28:12.757
To them, tilling is worse than...

00:28:12.757 --> 00:28:17.626
...the kind of destruction you
get from carpet-bombing in war.

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:19.931
But...

00:28:19.931 --> 00:28:24.334
...even the fields that are tilled
can yield some good crops.

00:28:24.936 --> 00:28:27.404
That's because they use fertilizers.

00:28:27.605 --> 00:28:31.376
To replace the nutrients that were
provided by the dead creatures.

00:28:31.376 --> 00:28:33.978
But by giving the soil fertilizer...

00:28:33.978 --> 00:28:37.345
...can't you get nice, big
vegetables and good rice?

00:28:37.682 --> 00:28:41.019
Of course, the plants will grow
well if you give the soil fertilizer.

00:28:41.019 --> 00:28:44.989
But what if you gave it
more than you had to...

00:28:44.989 --> 00:28:48.152
...and you just get vegetables
that are too big?

00:28:48.326 --> 00:28:49.588
Too big?

00:28:50.528 --> 00:28:52.630
That's never a problem.

00:28:52.630 --> 00:28:55.233
People always want
bigger vegetables.

00:28:55.233 --> 00:28:57.469
But if people get too big...

00:28:57.469 --> 00:28:59.571
...they get heavy and become slow.

00:28:59.571 --> 00:29:03.341
Well, that might be the
case with humans...

00:29:03.341 --> 00:29:06.578
Too much is as bad as too little,
they say.

00:29:06.578 --> 00:29:10.878
People and vegetables,
cows and pigs are all the same.

00:29:11.116 --> 00:29:15.120
With a lack of nutrition,
they get thin and weak...

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:17.554
...if there's too much,
they get too fat...

00:29:18.189 --> 00:29:19.554
...and get weak?

00:29:22.026 --> 00:29:23.962
They get weak...

00:29:23.962 --> 00:29:25.953
...and the bugs come...

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:29.729
When the wind blows,
the cooper benefits.

00:29:30.535 --> 00:29:33.671
If you till the land,
the soil becomes weak.

00:29:33.671 --> 00:29:36.975
Because the soil becomes weak,
fertilizers become necessary.

00:29:36.975 --> 00:29:40.345
The fields you give fertilizers to
get eaten up by insects.

00:29:40.345 --> 00:29:45.216
The more you overfeed livestock,
the more they will tend to become ill.

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:48.920
And in order to get rid
of those insects and viruses...

00:29:48.920 --> 00:29:50.522
...we spray the fields
with insecticide...

00:29:50.522 --> 00:29:52.786
...or give the livestock medicine.

00:29:53.057 --> 00:29:56.461
Vegetables and animals given too
much insecticide and medicine...

00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:58.588
...get weaker and weaker...

00:29:59.531 --> 00:30:01.599
They may look bigger...

00:30:01.599 --> 00:30:05.729
...but if people were to eat
crops that have gotten weaker...

00:30:06.738 --> 00:30:08.205
No...
